  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "associated-oyster-3ec6",
  "summary": "Recent resources pair cell-type-resolved annotations with GWAS, single-cell, spatial and drug-response data across thousands of samples.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is harmonizing heterogeneous omics data into queryable, cell-type-resolved resources. CellMethMarker provides 347,514 de novo and 2.2M literature-derived cell- and tissue-type methylation markers for deconvolution; scMRdb pairs 5206 GWAS summary statistics with 585 sc-eQTL datasets for cell-type-resolved Mendelian randomization; XYcellAtlas spans 6764 samples across 18 cancers, and mV2G integrates 24 functional evidence types across 50 tissues. CNVSIM, DiseaseCIO and RNAactDrug 2.0 extend this approach to copy-number subtypes, intervention outcomes and drug sensitivity features. A separate strand addresses fusion and chimeric RNA: RIFTT combines Arriba and FusionCatcher to reduce false positives, and a 569,640-chimera atlas across 1019 cancer cell lines links candidates to cell fitness. The contribution is mainly integration breadth and queryable access, with the chimeric RNA work adding dependency linkage.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
